  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>A warning first</h2>
      <p><strong>This lake is not an outing for your dog.</strong> The regulation published by the Provence Verte &amp; Verdon tourist office for Lac Sainte-Suzanne, known as "Lac de Carcès", is explicit: "pets banned around the lake".</p>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Nestled among the wooded hills of the Provence Verte, between Carcès and Cabasse, this body of water of around a hundred hectares is entirely devoted to walking and fishing: jogging, picnics, cycling, nature discovery and birdwatching.</p>
      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Besides the ban on pets, the site's regulation bans access to the water, swimming and boating on the lake (it is a drinking-water reserve for Toulon), wild camping, barbecues and fires, and flying recreational drones. Only line fishing is allowed, no-kill for carp and black bass. Access to the site is also subject to the summer restrictions on access to forest massifs. The lake car park is on the D24, towards Vins-sur-Caramy.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: I can't come along here, even on a leash. For a freshwater outing in the Var with me, look at the other listings in the area instead.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Carcès and the Caramy falls are close by; check their dog rules before going.</p>
